    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The intermittent nature strongly suggests a timing or state management issue, possibly a race condition in your backend session handling. If the first transaction succeeds, your backend might proceed to use old or inconsistent session data for the subsequent calls. To trace this, implement robust logging on your server to record the exact state of the session object *before* and *after* every Stripe API call. This will help determine if the state degrades between the successful and failed attempts.",
